# A subject of two letters that are not ASCII and 46 blanks. The blanks do
# not fit on the line, so they are all written inside encoded words of '_',
# 32 on the first line and 14 on the second. A blank kept in plain between
# two encoded words would be dropped by a reader (RFC 2047, 6.2). (With 45
# blanks they all fit on the first line, and none is lost.)
mode=accept
tls=none
form=(From=alice@example.com To=bob@example.net Body=$'Hi\n' User=alice Password=secret
      Subject="$(printf '\xc3\xa9\xc3\xa9')$(printf ' %.0s' $(seq 46))")
